      "raw_response": "ANSWER: REFUTED\n\nAccording to the abstract, sympathetic nerve activity is not reduced but rather increased throughout normal pregnancy, and even more so in hypertensive pregnancies. The findings suggest that sympathetic drive is impaired in normotensive nonpregnant women and even more so in women with PIH, contradicting the claim that sympathetic activity decreases during normal pregnancy. The increase in sympathetic activity in pregnant women seems to help maintain blood pressure within a normal range until late in the pregnancy when it becomes excessive and may lead to hypertension.",
